<h2>Reading a process change</h2>
<p>When a supplier changes a material, a coating parameter or a formation step, the effect appears in the end-of-line distribution before it appears in the field. Ask for the process change notice, the affected lots and the before/after test data. A change that is not documented is a change you cannot audit.</p>
<h2>The limits of a certificate</h2>
<p>A quality certificate covers the system, not the shipment. The batch COA covers the sample, not every cell. The only evidence that the shipment matches the sample is the traceability record between them — lot numbers, process parameters and end-of-line data. That is why the intermediate QC record is the most useful document a buyer can request.</p>
