<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<h3>What is the most common manufacturing defect?</h3>
<p>Inconsistent coating weight and poor weld or tab quality are the most common causes of early failure. Both are visible in process data before they reach the customer, which is why the intermediate QC record matters more than the final pass rate.</p>
<h3>Does a higher purity material always give a better battery?</h3>
<p>No. Purity matters, but particle size, morphology and the matching of cathode, anode and electrolyte determine performance. A high-purity material in a poorly matched design can underperform a well-matched standard material.</p>
